{"id": 36, "ts": 1780440286.1909165, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I understand that both Sarah and Emily have expressed confidence in Candidate\u202fC, likely drawn to his quick decision\u2011making, calmness in a crisis, and strong technical grasp. However, the same notes also flag serious crew\u2011cooperation concerns: C is described as egocentric, has difficulty communicating ideas, and is not very willing to pursue further education. In a long\u2011distance cockpit, the ability to collaborate, share information clearly, and stay open to feedback is essential for safety. By contrast, Candidate\u202fB is noted as very conscientious, handles stress very well, and excels at assessing weather\u2014key reliability and stress\u2011resilience factors for international routes. While B does have a weak memory for numbers and has made some nasty remarks, the memory issue can be mitigated with standard check\u2011list procedures, and the remarks, though concerning, have not been characterized as pervasive hostility. Given the balance of operational reliability and stress resilience versus the interpersonal deficits that could undermine crew dynamics, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the stronger overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
